@inject ApiMetadata Api
@* Form's Overview, written by hand after Button's: fields, what posting needs, errors and columns
   previewed in each mode, labels beside fields, read-only, then a validator of your own and files
   as code. The Forms and validation article covers the model's attributes at more length.
   Accessibility and See also come from the doc comment. *@

<Heading Level="2">Usage</Heading>
<Code Block Language="razor">@Usage</Code>
<TextBlock>A form is a set of fields bound to a model, which it validates and submits to your handler. It suits any data the user enters and saves. It works the same on <Anchor Href="docs/common/render-modes">static pages</Anchor> and interactive pages. <Anchor Href="docs/common/forms">Forms and validation</Anchor> covers the model's attributes at more length.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Fields</Heading>
<TextBlock>Each field in a form is bound to a property of the model, and gets its label, required mark, type and limits from the property's attributes. Bind each field with <Code>@@bind-Value</Code>. The fields post with the form.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="home-settings" />
<TextBlock><Anchor Href="docs/common/forms">Forms and validation</Anchor> lists what each attribute does.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Posting and submitting</Heading>
<TextBlock>On static pages, a form post fills the model only when the form and the model property share a name. Set <Code>FormName</Code> on the form, and <Code>[SupplyParameterFromForm]</Code> with the same name on the property (<Anchor Href="docs/troubleshooting/form-name">what goes wrong without it</Anchor>).</TextBlock>
<Prose Class="site-table ib-scroll">
    <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Handler</th><th>Runs</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr><td><Code>OnValidSubmit</Code></td><td>When the model is valid, in every render mode</td></tr>
            <tr><td><Code>OnInvalidSubmit</Code></td><td>When the model isn't valid</td></tr>
            <tr><td><Code>OnSubmit</Code></td><td>In place of both, when you validate yourself</td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
</Prose>
<List>
    <ListItem>On static pages, the form post is a real one. Blazor's enhanced form handling sends it without a full reload.</ListItem>
    <ListItem>With JavaScript off, the browser posts the form and loads the page. To always load the page, set <Code>Enhance="false"</Code>.</ListItem>
    <ListItem>On interactive pages, the form submits to C#, with no form post.</ListItem>
</List>

<Heading Level="2">Errors</Heading>
<TextBlock>An error summary lists every message at the top of the form after a failed submit. It receives focus, so keyboard and screen reader users start there. Add a <Code>FormErrors</Code> at the top of the form. To skip the browser's checks so the server's messages show at once, set <Code>NativeValidation="false"</Code>.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="form-errors" />
<TextBlock>Each field shows its own messages under it too. To show one property's messages beside an input of your own, add <Code>FieldError For="() =&gt; Model.Email" Id="email-error"</Code>, and set the input's <Code>aria-describedby</Code> to that <Code>Id</Code>.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Columns</Heading>
<TextBlock>A form can lay its fields out in columns that fit the form's own width, so one form works on a page, in a dialog and in a drawer. Set <Code>Columns</Code>, up to 4. To give a field the whole row, set <Code>ColSpan="GridSpan.Full"</Code> on it.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="form-columns" />
<TextBlock>Two columns start at 32rem, three at 48rem and four at 64rem. <Code>FormActions</Code>, <Code>FormErrors</Code> and anything else that isn't a field fill the whole row.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Labels beside fields</Heading>
<TextBlock>A horizontal form puts each label beside its field from 640px up, rather than above it. Set <Code>Layout="FormLayout.Horizontal"</Code>. To choose the marks on fields, set <Code>RequiredMark</Code>: an asterisk on required fields (the default), "(optional)" on the others as in this example, or none.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="form-horizontal" />

<Heading Level="2">Read-only and disabled</Heading>
<TextBlock>A read-only form shows a record that posts but can't change, and a disabled form turns every field off. Set <Code>ReadOnly</Code> or <Code>Disabled</Code>. Disabled fields don't post. Neither changes the buttons, so show the ones that fit.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="form-read-only" />
<List>
    <ListItem>HTML has no read-only select, checkbox, radio or range. A read-only select shows its value in a read-only text field. Checkboxes, switches, radios, segments and sliders are disabled, and hidden fields post their values.</ListItem>
    <ListItem>Before trusting a posted value, see <Anchor Href="docs/common/forms#values-a-form-post-can-change">Values a form post can change</Anchor>. Before saving a disabled value from a form post, see <Anchor Href="docs/common/forms#disabled-fields-and-form-posts">Disabled fields and form posts</Anchor>.</ListItem>
</List>

<Heading Level="2">Custom validation</Heading>
<TextBlock>A form validates with DataAnnotations by default. To use another validator, such as FluentValidation, set <Code>Validator</Code>. To work with the edit context yourself, pass an <Code>EditContext</Code> in place of <Code>Model</Code>.</TextBlock>
<Code Block Language="razor">@Validation</Code>

<Heading Level="2">Files</Heading>
<TextBlock>A form with a <Anchor Href="docs/components/file-upload">FileUpload</Anchor> must send its fields as multipart data, or a form post on static pages sends only the files' names. Set <Code>Multipart</Code> on the form.</TextBlock>
<Code Block Language="razor">@Files</Code>

<Heading Level="2">Labels and localization</Heading>
<TextBlock>The error summary has a heading of its own. The words for marks on fields, such as "(required)" and "(optional)", have no parameter. To set them for the whole app, see <Anchor Href="docs/common/text">Text and other languages</Anchor>.</TextBlock>
<Prose Class="site-table ib-scroll">
    <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Sets</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr><td><Code>Title</Code></td><td>The <Code>FormErrors</Code> summary's heading</td><td>"Please fix the following"</td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
</Prose>

@if (OverviewParts.Of(Component, Api).Count > 0)
{
    <Heading Level="2">Parts</Heading>
}
<OverviewParts Component="Component" />

<Heading Level="2">Mode support</Heading>
<ModeSupportTable Component="Component" ApiComponent="ApiComponent" />

@if (ApiComponent.Accessibility is not null)
{
    <Heading Level="2">Accessibility</Heading>
    <DocHtml Html="@ApiComponent.Accessibility" Context="@(Context with { Overview = true })" Size="ProseSize.Md" />
}

<Heading Level="2">Parameters</Heading>
<ParameterTable ApiComponent="ApiComponent" ApiHref="@Registry.ApiPageHref(Component)" Context="Context" Compact />

<OverviewSeeAlso Component="Component" ApiComponent="ApiComponent" />

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public RegistryComponent Component { get; set; } = null!;

    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public ApiComponent ApiComponent { get; set; } = null!;

    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public ApiPageContext Context { get; set; } = null!;

    private const string Usage = """
        <Form Model="Profile" FormName="profile" OnValidSubmit="SaveAsync">
            <FormErrors />
            <TextField @bind-Value="Profile!.Name" />
            <TextField @bind-Value="Profile!.Email" />
            <FormActions><Button Submit>Save</Button></FormActions>
        </Form>

        @code {
            // A post on a static page fills it; the same name as FormName.
            [SupplyParameterFromForm(FormName = "profile")]
            private ProfileModel? Profile { get; set; }

            protected override void OnInitialized() => Profile ??= new();
        }
        """;

    private const string Validation = """
        @* Blazored.FluentValidation's validator, in place of DataAnnotations. *@
        <Form Model="Order" FormName="order" OnValidSubmit="PlaceAsync">
            <Validator><FluentValidationValidator /></Validator>
            ...
        </Form>
        """;

    private const string Files = """
        <Form Model="Profile" FormName="profile" Multipart OnValidSubmit="SaveAsync">
            <FileUpload Name="Avatar" Label="Profile photo" Accept=".png,.jpg" MaxFileSize="2_000_000" />
            <FormActions><Button Submit>Save</Button></FormActions>
        </Form>

        @code {
            [SupplyParameterFromForm(FormName = "profile")]
            private ProfileModel? Profile { get; set; }

            // The file, named like the field.
            [SupplyParameterFromForm(FormName = "profile")]
            private IFormFile? Avatar { get; set; }

            protected override void OnInitialized() => Profile ??= new();
        }
        """;
}
